         filled, since the splash screen never fills this shape either, it only ever calls
         drawPath(..., style = Stroke(...)) on it. Filling any dilated/offset copy of a thin
         script glyph like this risks the offset self-intersecting and the fill rule solidifying
         the whole letterform instead of staying a hollow tube, which is what a filled version of
         this shape ran into. Stroking the single original path at increasing widths (fillColor
         transparent throughout) can't have that problem, and reads exactly like the splash's own
